<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Continental System</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1806">1806</a>–<a href="/years/1814">1814</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Continental Blockade</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Continental System was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s embargo on British trade, decreed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> in 1806 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> in 1807, which forbade <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, its allies and dependent states from trading with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. It aimed to ruin the British economy but caused shortages and widespread smuggling, hurt continental ports and industries, and its enforcement led to Napoleon's war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> in 1812.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/continental-system.jpg" alt="Continental System" width="320" height="325" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TRAJAN 117 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Continental_Blockade_(1812).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
